@lang en

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `uk-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `uk-interpretation-application`

-- The Interpretation Act 1978 (1978 c. 30): the general provisions that the other modules do not hold.
-- Section 1, section 14A(6), section 22(2), section 23(2), the second limb of section 23(3), and section 25(2) read in full.
--
-- Source: the converter-made plain-text rendering in ../../registers/source-bundle/ukpga-1978-30.txt, not the official text (see SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
--
-- A boolean named "... provides that ..." answers TRUE when the section says so and FALSE when it does not say so; FALSE never means that
-- the opposite is the law. Where the text points at a rule it does not give (the provision of this Act that "corresponds" to a provision
-- of the Interpretation Act 1889), the function refuses by name and the tests assert the refusal.

§ `Nouns of this module`

-- The events that the Act speaks of when it speaks of an enactment's life, and the names it gives them for subordinate legislation (fork F25).
DECLARE `Event in the life of an enactment` IS ONE OF
    `its passing`
    `its repeal`

DECLARE `Name the Act gives to an event` IS ONE OF
    `passing`
    `making`
    `repeal`
    `revocation`
    `enactment of the Measure or Act`

DECLARE `Where a period or day is specified` IS ONE OF
    `in the subordinate legislation`
    `in the Act that confers the power or duty`
    `in some other instrument`

§ `Named refusals of this module`

-- A refusal is an expression at any type; each name is its message.

-- src:214 | (2) Without prejudice to section 17(2)(a), a reference to the Interpretation Act 1889, to any provision of that Act or to any other enactment repealed by this Act, whether occurring in another Act, in subordinate legislation, in Northern Ireland legislation or in any deed or other instrument or document, shall be construed as referring to this Act, or to the corresponding provision of this Act, as it applies to Acts passed at the time of the reference.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 25(2) (src:214): "the corresponding provision of this Act": no provision of this Act or of Schedule 3 says which provision corresponds to a provision of the 1889 Act
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 25(2) does not say which provision of the Interpretation Act 1978 corresponds to a provision of the Interpretation Act 1889 or of another enactment it repeals` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 25(2) does not say which provision of the Interpretation Act 1978 corresponds to a provision of the Interpretation Act 1889 or of another enactment it repeals"

§ `Section 1: words of enactment`

-- src:6 | 1 Words of enactment.
-- src:7 | Every section of an Act takes effect as a substantive enactment without introductory words.
-- src:396 | Section 1
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 1 (src:6-7), with Sch 2 para 2 (src:396): the section reaches Acts passed after the year 1850
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `it is a section of an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the section has introductory words` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 1 provides that a section of an Act takes effect as a substantive enactment, for an Act passed on` day `it is a section of an Act` `the section has introductory words` MEANS
        `it is a section of an Act`
    AND ((`the extent to which the provision applies to an Act passed on` `section 1` day) EQUALS `applies without limit`)

§ `Section 14A(6): "specified"`

-- src:58 | (6) In this section, “specified” means specified in the subordinate legislation.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 14A(6) (src:58): "specified" means specified in the subordinate legislation
GIVEN where IS A `Where a period or day is specified`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 14A(6) counts the period or day as specified` where MEANS
    CONSIDER where
    WHEN `in the subordinate legislation` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `in the Act that confers the power or duty` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `in some other instrument` THEN FALSE

§ `Section 22(2): a reference to an Act`

DECLARE `Kind of reference in the Act` IS ONE OF
    `a reference to an Act in a provision`
    `a reference to an enactment`
    `a reference in section 19(1) to other Acts`

-- "In any of the foregoing provisions of this Act a reference to an Act is a reference to an Act to which that provision applies; but this does not
-- affect the generality of references to enactments or of the references in section 19(1) to other Acts." A provision that applies to an Act in part
-- applies to it; only `does not apply` leaves the Act out.
-- src:104 | (2) In any of the foregoing provisions of this Act a reference to an Act is a reference to an Act to which that provision applies; but this does not affect the generality of references to enactments or of the references in section 19(1) to other Acts.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 22(2) (src:104)
GIVEN kind      IS A `Kind of reference in the Act`
      provision IS A `Provision of the Act`
      day       IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 22(2) reads the reference as reaching an Act passed on` kind provision day MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `a reference to an Act in a provision` THEN NOT ((`the extent to which the provision applies to an Act passed on` provision day) EQUALS `does not apply`)
    WHEN `a reference to an enactment` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a reference in section 19(1) to other Acts` THEN TRUE

§ `Section 23(2) and section 23(3): enactments comprised in subordinate legislation`

-- "In the application of this Act to Acts passed or subordinate legislation made after the commencement of this Act, all references to an enactment
-- include an enactment comprised in subordinate legislation whenever made". The enactment that the Act is applied to is `e`; for an earlier one the
-- subsection gives nothing and the caller's answer apart from it stands.
-- src:108 | (2) In the application of this Act to Acts passed or subordinate legislation made after the commencement of this Act, all references to an enactment include an enactment comprised in subordinate legislation whenever made, and references to the passing or repeal of an enactment are to be construed accordingly.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 23(2) (src:108)
GIVEN e IS AN `An enactment`
      `it is an enactment apart from this subsection` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is comprised in subordinate legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 23(2) counts the thing as an enactment` e `it is an enactment apart from this subsection` `it is comprised in subordinate legislation` MEANS
    IF   `the day is on or after the commencement of the Interpretation Act 1978` (e's `the day it was passed or made`)
    THEN `it is an enactment apart from this subsection` OR `it is comprised in subordinate legislation`
    ELSE `it is an enactment apart from this subsection`

-- "and references to the passing or repeal of an enactment are to be construed accordingly": for an enactment comprised in subordinate legislation
-- the passing is the making of that legislation and the repeal its revocation. The Act does not itself name "making" and "revocation" here (fork F25).
-- src:108 | (2) In the application of this Act to Acts passed or subordinate legislation made after the commencement of this Act, all references to an enactment include an enactment comprised in subordinate legislation whenever made, and references to the passing or repeal of an enactment are to be construed accordingly.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 23(2) (src:108): "references to the passing or repeal of an enactment are to be construed accordingly"
GIVEN event IS AN `Event in the life of an enactment`
GIVETH A `Name the Act gives to an event`
`section 23(2) names the event for an enactment comprised in subordinate legislation as` event MEANS
    CONSIDER event
    WHEN `its passing` THEN `making`
    WHEN `its repeal`  THEN `revocation`

-- "in the application of section 17(2)(a) to Acts passed or subordinate legislation made after the commencement of this Act, the reference to any other
-- enactment includes any deed or other instrument or document." The first limb of s 23(3) is in uk-interpretation-application.l4.
-- src:109 | (3) Sections 9 and 19(1) also apply to deeds and other instruments and documents as they apply to Acts and subordinate legislation; and in the application of section 17(2)(a) to Acts passed or subordinate legislation made after the commencement of this Act, the reference to any other enactment includes any deed or other instrument or document.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 23(3) (src:109): the second limb
GIVEN e IS AN `An enactment`
      `it is an other enactment apart from this limb` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a deed or other instrument or document` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 23(3) counts the thing as an other enactment in section 17(2)(a)` e `it is an other enactment apart from this limb` `it is a deed or other instrument or document` MEANS
    IF   `the day is on or after the commencement of the Interpretation Act 1978` (e's `the day it was passed or made`)
    THEN `it is an other enactment apart from this limb` OR `it is a deed or other instrument or document`
    ELSE `it is an other enactment apart from this limb`

§ `Section 25(2): references to the Interpretation Act 1889 and to other repealed enactments`

-- "a reference to the Interpretation Act 1889, to any provision of that Act or to any other enactment repealed by this Act ... shall be construed as referring to
-- this Act, or to the corresponding provision of this Act, as it applies to Acts passed at the time of the reference."
-- The Act does not say which provision corresponds to which, so the caller names it; what the Act gives is the second half: the corresponding provision "as it
-- applies to Acts passed at the time of the reference", which is the extent to which that provision reaches an Act passed on the day of the reference.
-- src:214 | (2) Without prejudice to section 17(2)(a), a reference to the Interpretation Act 1889, to any provision of that Act or to any other enactment repealed by this Act, whether occurring in another Act, in subordinate legislation, in Northern Ireland legislation or in any deed or other instrument or document, shall be construed as referring to this Act, or to the corresponding provision of this Act, as it applies to Acts passed at the time of the reference.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 25(2) (src:214): "as it applies to Acts passed at the time of the reference"
GIVEN provision IS A `Provision of the Act`
      `the day of the reference` IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `Extent of application`
`section 25(2) — the extent to which the corresponding provision applies to a reference made on` provision `the day of the reference` MEANS
    `the extent to which the provision applies to an Act passed on` provision `the day of the reference`

-- src:214 | (2) Without prejudice to section 17(2)(a), a reference to the Interpretation Act 1889, to any provision of that Act or to any other enactment repealed by this Act, whether occurring in another Act, in subordinate legislation, in Northern Ireland legislation or in any deed or other instrument or document, shall be construed as referring to this Act, or to the corresponding provision of this Act, as it applies to Acts passed at the time of the reference.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 25(2) (src:214): "to the corresponding provision of this Act"
GIVEN `the provision of the Interpretation Act 1889 or of another repealed enactment that is referred to` IS A STRING
GIVETH A `Provision of the Act`
`section 25(2) — the corresponding provision of the Interpretation Act 1978` `the provision of the Interpretation Act 1889 or of another repealed enactment that is referred to` MEANS
    `section 25(2) does not say which provision of the Interpretation Act 1978 corresponds to a provision of the Interpretation Act 1889 or of another enactment it repeals`
